### =====================================================================
### appointMe - day18-conflicts.http   (Day 18: clean 409s, cancel, reschedule, working hours)
### SELF-CONTAINED: it logs in by itself and keeps its own tokens.
###
### BEFORE YOU START (and before every re-run of this file)
###   1. Put the NEW scripts/dev-seed.sql in place (it now gives tenant 2's Bob working hours too).
###   2. Reload it:
###        Get-Content .\scripts\dev-seed.sql | docker exec -i appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme
###
### Cast (password for all: correct-horse-1)
###   ALICE = OWNER of tenant 1, membership 1, works Mon-Fri 09:00-17:00 (Athens time)
###   BOB   = STAFF in tenant 1, membership 2, works Mon-Fri 09:00-13:00 and 14:00-18:00
### All bookings are on Tuesday 2027-02-09. Haircut = 30 minutes, customer 1.
### Times below are UTC (Z). Athens is UTC+2 in February, so:
###   07:00Z = 09:00 local   10:00Z = 12:00 local   11:00Z = 13:00 local (lunch)   12:00Z = 14:00 local
### Sunday 2027-02-14: nobody works.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080


### ======================================================================
### SETUP
### ======================================================================

### O1. Alice logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### O2. Alice selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### W1. Bob logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("bobUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### W2. Bob selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, STAFF
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bobUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}


### ======================================================================
### B. DOUBLE-BOOKING IS NOW A CLEAN 409
### ======================================================================

### B1. Book Bob 10:00Z-10:30Z (12:00 local). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z", "notes": "b1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("b1Id", response.body.id);
    client.test("B1: booked", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### B2. EXACTLY the same slot. EXPECT 409 with the SPECIFIC message (Day 17 gave you a generic one)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z", "notes": "duplicate" }

> {%
    client.test("B2: 409, slot already booked", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail === "That time slot is already booked for this staff member",
            "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### B3. Partial overlap, 10:15Z. EXPECT 409, same message
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:15:00Z", "notes": "overlap" }

> {%
    client.test("B3: 409, slot already booked", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail === "That time slot is already booked for this staff member",
            "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### B4. Back-to-back, 10:30Z-11:00Z (12:30-13:00 local, ends exactly at closing). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:30:00Z", "notes": "b4" }

> {%
    client.global.set("b4Id", response.body.id);
    client.test("B4: back-to-back allowed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### B5. Alice (a different staff member) at the same time. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 1, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z", "notes": "alice" }

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceApptId", response.body.id);
    client.test("B5: other staff allowed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### W. WORKING HOURS ARE ENFORCED WHEN BOOKING
### ======================================================================

### W1. 06:00Z = 08:00 local, before Bob starts at 09:00. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T06:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W1: before opening", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail === "The staff member does not work at that time",
            "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### W2. 11:00Z = 13:00 local, Bob's lunch break. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T11:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W2: lunch break", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W3. 10:45Z = 12:45 local: 30 minutes would end at 13:15, after the morning window closes. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:45:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W3: straddles closing time", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W4. 12:00Z = 14:00 local, the very start of the afternoon window. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T12:00:00Z", "notes": "w4" }

> {%
    client.global.set("w4Id", response.body.id);
    client.test("W4: exactly at reopening", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W5. Sunday 2027-02-14: Bob has no hours that day. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-14T10:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W5: day off", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W6. In the past. EXPECT 400 with errors.startsAt (the @Future check on the DTO still runs first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2020-01-07T10:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W6: past", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W7. Another tenant's customer (customer 3), at a valid time. EXPECT 404
###     (the ownership lookups run BEFORE the working-hours check)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 3, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T08:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W7: foreign customer is a 404, not a working-hours error", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### W8. Alice outside HER hours: 15:30Z = 17:30 local, she finishes at 17:00. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 1, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T15:30:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("W8: after Alice's closing time", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### X. CANCEL   (PATCH /appointments/{id}/cancel)
### ======================================================================

### X1. Cancel B1. EXPECT 200, status CANCELLED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{b1Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("X1: cancelled", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.status === "CANCELLED", "status field " + response.body.status);
    });
%}

### X2. Cancel it again. EXPECT 409 (only SCHEDULED appointments can be cancelled)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{b1Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("X2: already cancelled", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail.indexOf("Only SCHEDULED") === 0, "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### X3. The freed slot can be booked again (10:00Z). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z", "notes": "x3" }

> {%
    client.global.set("x3Id", response.body.id);
    client.test("X3: slot reused", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### X4. Mark the new one COMPLETED (Day 9 endpoint). EXPECT 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{x3Id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "COMPLETED" }

### X5. Cancel a COMPLETED appointment. EXPECT 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{x3Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("X5: completed cannot be cancelled", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### X6. An id that does not exist. EXPECT 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/99999/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### X7. Bob (STAFF) cancels ALICE's appointment. EXPECT 404 (not his, so it "does not exist" for him)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{aliceApptId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

> {%
    client.test("X7: staff cannot touch a colleague's appointment", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### X8. Bob cancels his OWN afternoon appointment (W4). EXPECT 200, CANCELLED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{w4Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

> {%
    client.test("X8: staff cancels own", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.status === "CANCELLED", "status field " + response.body.status);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### R. RESCHEDULE   (PATCH /appointments/{id}/reschedule, body: { "startsAt": ... })
### The length of the appointment is kept (30 minutes). The end is recomputed.
### ======================================================================

### R0. A fresh appointment for Bob at 07:00Z (09:00 local). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-09T07:00:00Z", "notes": "to be moved" }

> {%
    client.global.set("rId", response.body.id);
    client.test("R0: booked", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### R1. Move it 15 minutes later: 07:15Z. The new time OVERLAPS ITS OWN old time, which is fine.
###     EXPECT 200, startsAt 2027-02-09T07:15:00Z, endsAt 2027-02-09T07:45:00Z
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T07:15:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R1: moved, length kept", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.startsAt === "2027-02-09T07:15:00Z", "startsAt " + response.body.startsAt);
        client.assert(response.body.endsAt === "2027-02-09T07:45:00Z", "endsAt " + response.body.endsAt);
    });
%}

### R2. Move it onto 10:00Z, which Bob's COMPLETED appointment (X3) still occupies. EXPECT 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R2: target slot taken", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail === "That time slot is already booked for this staff member",
            "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### R3. A failed reschedule changes NOTHING. EXPECT 200, startsAt still 2027-02-09T07:15:00Z
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("R3: unchanged after the failure", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.startsAt === "2027-02-09T07:15:00Z", "startsAt " + response.body.startsAt);
    });
%}

### R4. Move to 05:00Z = 07:00 local, before Bob works. EXPECT 409 "does not work at that time"
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T05:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R4: outside working hours", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail === "The staff member does not work at that time",
            "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### R5. Move to the past. EXPECT 400, message mentions the future
###     (this DTO has no @Future: the SERVICE enforces it, so it works for any caller)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2020-01-07T10:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R5: past", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail.indexOf("future") >= 0, "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### R6. Reschedule a CANCELLED appointment (B1). EXPECT 409 "Only SCHEDULED appointments can be rescheduled"
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{b1Id}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T08:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R6: cancelled cannot be moved", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail.indexOf("Only SCHEDULED") === 0, "detail was: " + response.body.detail);
    });
%}

### R7. Missing "startsAt". EXPECT 400 with errors.startsAt
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ }

> {%
    client.test("R7: validation", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.errors && response.body.errors.startsAt, "errors.startsAt missing");
    });
%}

### R8. Bob (STAFF) tries to move ALICE's appointment. EXPECT 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{aliceApptId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T08:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R8: not his appointment", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### R9. Bob moves his OWN appointment to 07:30Z. EXPECT 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T07:30:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R9: staff moves own", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.startsAt === "2027-02-09T07:30:00Z", "startsAt " + response.body.startsAt);
    });
%}

### R10. Move to Sunday 2027-02-14 (nobody works). EXPECT 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-14T10:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R10: day off", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### R11. The OWNER may move Bob's appointment: 08:00Z (10:00 local). EXPECT 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{rId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2027-02-09T08:00:00Z" }

> {%
    client.test("R11: owner moves it", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.startsAt === "2027-02-09T08:00:00Z", "startsAt " + response.body.startsAt);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### F. FINAL STATE
### ======================================================================

### F1. Everything on 2027-02-09 (owner). EXPECT 200 and 6 appointments:
###     b1 CANCELLED 10:00Z | b4 10:30Z | Alice 10:00Z | w4 CANCELLED 12:00Z | x3 COMPLETED 10:00Z | moved one 08:00Z
GET {{baseUrl}}/appointments?from=2027-02-09T00:00:00Z&to=2027-02-10T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("F1: six appointments", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 6, "count " + response.body.length);
    });
%}

### The database's view (run in PowerShell, not here):
###   docker exec -it appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme -c "SELECT id, staff_id, starts_at, ends_at, status, notes, version FROM appointments WHERE starts_at::date = '2027-02-09' ORDER BY staff_id, starts_at;"
### The moved appointment has version > 0 (each update bumps it). Rejected attempts left no trace.
